# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 102.6 min of real streamed gameplay, o:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with the step tolerance on at its default of 18% and the long-gap rule on at its default of 100 ms (neither typed), through Windows.Graphics.Capture, with the synthesized presents drawn by the optical flow warp and its cut gate, or the blend across a gap over 100 ms, through the second capture card, 2026-11-14, build d4d6001; cut to the gameplay the stream's video shows, 69.6 s to 6224.9 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 102.6 min of real streamed gameplay, o:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with the step tolerance on at its default of 18% and the long-gap rule on at its default of 100 ms (neither typed), through Windows.Graphics.Capture, with the synthesized presents drawn by the optical flow warp and its cut gate, or the blend across a gap over 100 ms, through the second capture card, 2026-11-14, build d4d6001; cut to the gameplay the stream's video shows, 69.6 s to 6224.9 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 60
field_long_runs 1
field_synth_pct 1.5
field_pull_wraps 161
# WHAT IT COVERS: the second of two 2026-11-14 streams, 102.6 minutes cut to the gameplay its
# video shows, captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on d4d6001, the step
# tolerance at 18% and the long-gap rule at 100 ms, the same launch as 2026-11-13. It carries
# step_tolerance_pct 18. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 1121 times (656 an hour) and stalled
# for 100 ms or more 124 times (73 an hour), in 145 bursts, 47 of them with a stall; the longest
# stalls are 878 ms at about 2215 s, 863 ms at about 161 s and 784 ms at about 3063 s. No
# periodic stretch. Two tournament fights run the game below 60 fps for seconds at a time,
# 4306 s to 4317 s and 5555 s to 5559 s. The lock released 11 times. The worst blend run, 60
# presents, the first run of 50 or more on a stream since the step tolerance, starts at
# 3011.86 s in steady footage, 30 s after the last hitch, with the lock held at its start and
# released inside it; the second worst, 37, starts at 4614.10 s.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 69.552 s, from the 1260
# marked frames in its first 21 s, matched within 0.36 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 6155.4 s with no holes; it opens on gameplay, a conversation and the dice game's selection
# screen and ends on gameplay, so the cut is its whole span, 69.6 s to 6224.9 s. Inside the cut,
# 53 seconds in 35 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime: 33 single hitch seconds and the two
# fights above (12 s and 5 s), which are gameplay. The pause menu is open for about 2 s just
# after the first fight.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships (the split-pair rule added since is off
# by default and off here), with the step tolerance at the setting the key names, so the two
# lines are comparable. The replay line (the plain arm, no dejitter) reads synth 1.5% against
# 1.5%, worst run 37 against 60, runs >= 50 0 against 1 and pull wraps 161 against 161. On the
# dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, synth 1.5%, runs >= 50 1 and the worst run 60,
# starting at the same present as the field's, hence max_worst_run_dejit 60 beside the plain
# arm's 37; max_long_runs bounds the plain arm only. Counted over the window on the dejitter
# arm, replay against field: synthesized presents 5449 against 5461, repeats 876 against 870,
# skips 454 against 452. The replay makes 49 moves, 20 of them late, and 9 land more than 2 ms
# from a real frame; the field made 47 inside the window. The lock released 11 times in the
# field and 10 on the replay, the 10 within 0.50 ms; the field's eleventh, at 1262.95 s, follows
# a lock move 0.25 s after a 22 ms hitch, and the replay holds the lock there. The planner at
# 100 ms draws 707 synthesized presents over 144 pairs as the blend; the field drew 713 over
# the same 144 pairs.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 37
max_worst_run_dejit 60
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.9
min_reseeds 335
max_pull_wraps 161
compositor interp
extra_lag_ms 75
step_tolerance_pct 18
arrivals 732422
